-- #1094 ACCEPT half, and the "feature + UNRELATED code still behaves" fixture
-- (AGENTS.md: the assertion is deliberately about code that does NOT use the new
-- machinery).  Everything below must check clean.
--
-- Three things it pins, in order of how easy each is to break with a naive
-- "both index rows must be closed and equal" check written at the top of unify:
--
-- 1. INSTANTIATION IS NOT INTERCHANGE.  `pureBox`'s written closed `<>` meets the
--    FRESH OPEN effvar that instantiating `MkBox`'s scheme mints.  That is the
--    open~closed arm — solving a metavariable, not comparing two written rows — and
--    it must keep working.  (Same shape as `mkPure : a -> Async <> a` in
--    graded_closed_row_grade_ok.mdk, the fixture most likely to catch a botched fix.)
-- 2. EQUAL closed index rows still unify.  Invariance rejects DIFFERENT rows, not
--    every written one: `alsoLoud = loud` at `Box <Stdout> Unit` is fine.
-- 3. A row-POLYMORPHIC index still generalises and instantiates freely (`unbox`,
--    `mkBox`, `relay`), including against an open-tailed written row (`widen`).
--
-- The unrelated half — `Pair`, `Swapper`, `firstOf`, `idString` — mentions no effect
-- row, no index, and no `Box`.  Its inferred schemes are in this fixture's golden, so
-- a change that perturbs ordinary elaboration shows up here even though none of that
-- code goes near the index unifier.
data Box e a = MkBox (Unit -> <e> a)

unbox : Box e a -> <e> a
unbox (MkBox t) = t ()

mkBox : (Unit -> <e> a) -> Box e a
mkBox t = MkBox t

relay : Box e a -> Box e a
relay b = b

-- (1) written closed `<>` against the fresh index var from MkBox's scheme
pureBox : Unit -> Box <> Unit
pureBox u = MkBox (v => ())

shout : Unit -> <Stdout> Unit
shout u = shout u

loud : Box <Stdout> Unit
loud = MkBox shout

-- (2) equal closed index rows
alsoLoud : Box <Stdout> Unit
alsoLoud = loud

-- (3) an OPEN-tailed written index absorbs a narrower one
widen : Box <Stdout | e> Unit -> Box <Stdout | e> Unit
widen b = b

-- ── unrelated: nothing here mentions Box, an effect row, or an index ──────────
data Pair a b = MkPair a b

interface Swapper t where
  swap : t a b -> t b a

impl Swapper Pair where
  swap (MkPair a b) = MkPair b a

firstOf : Pair a b -> a
firstOf (MkPair a _) = a

idString : String -> String
idString s = s
